.TH COUNT_FILES 1 "October 2026" "count-files 2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
count_files \- count files in a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B count_files [directory]
.br
.B count_files \-h

.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts regular files, directories and symbolic links in a directory and all its subdirectories.
Also counts files with a given extension and shows the total size of the files and
the biggest file.
.PP
The extension is entered by the user when the program starts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Show help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/count_files.conf
Configuration file. The variable DEFAULT_DIR sets the default directory.

.SH EXAMPLES
Count files in the default directory:
.PP
.nf
count_files
.fi
.PP
Count files in the given directory:
.PP
.nf
count_files /var/log
.fi
.PP
Show help:
.PP
.nf
count_files \-h
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The program finished successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The specified directory doesn't exist.

.SH AUTHOR
Zlata Zadumina

